{"id":43999953006244,"type":"album","name":"Butterfly","artist":"Mariah Carey","year":1997,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710608.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-58250079-bbef-4c46-a59c-0e0622f8bdb1/mbid-58250079-bbef-4c46-a59c-0e0622f8bdb1-1728164950.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":12,"country":"US","aoty":59,"aoty_user":84,"yt":"FM75wg-I3dU","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/mariah-carey/butterfly-4","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/12433-mariah-carey-butterfly.php"},"desc":"Butterfly is the sixth studio album by American singer Mariah Carey, released on September 16, 1997, through Columbia Records. Widely regarded as one of her most personal and transformative works, Butterfly marked Carey’s full transition into R&B and hip-hop, leaving behind much of her adult contemporary roots. The album was met with critical and commercial success, solidifying her influence on the evolving landscape of late-90s pop and R&B. Background and Creation During the creation of Butterfly, Carey was undergoing a period of personal and professional reinvention. Her marriage to Sony executive Tommy Mottola was dissolving, giving her more creative control ."},"artist_ref":{"id":179950077316763,"name":"Mariah Carey","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mariah_Carey_Library_of_Congress_2023_2_%28cropped%2902.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":30277598324326,"type":"genre","name":"pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1523,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":44294165522841,"type":"genre","name":"r&b","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":908,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":176578125596945,"type":"genre","name":"Contemporary R&B","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":327,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":242048506390872,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Soul","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":250,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":50337978407967,"type":"genre","name":"Smooth Soul","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":